stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    [*] --> Poster

    Poster: Poster shown
    Poster: preload="none" · nothing streamed

    state reduced_check <<choice>>
    Poster --> reduced_check : mounted
    reduced_check --> Static : prefers-reduced-motion = reduce
    reduced_check --> Observing : motion allowed

    Static: Poster only — permanent
    Static: never streams, never animates

    Observing: Waiting on IntersectionObserver
    Observing: still nothing streamed

    Observing --> Loading : scrolled into view
    Loading: fetch webm → mp4 fallback

    state play_result <<choice>>
    Loading --> play_result : play() called
    play_result --> Playing : resolved
    play_result --> Blocked : rejected

    Playing: Silent loop
    Playing: burned-in subtitles carry the narration

    Blocked: Autoplay refused
    Blocked: iOS Low Power Mode — poster stays visible

    Playing --> Paused : scrolled out of view
    Paused --> Playing : scrolled back in

    Playing --> [*] : unmount — observer disconnected
    Paused --> [*] : unmount — observer disconnected
    Static --> [*] : unmount
    Blocked --> [*] : unmount

    note right of Blocked
        Treated as a supported state,
        not an error path.
        The poster is the real fallback.
    end note

    note right of Observing
        Guard: no IntersectionObserver
        (jsdom, old Safari) degrades
        to Static rather than throwing.
    end note
